Verdict: PASS. The change does what #1214 asked, and I confirmed it by running the built binary, not just by reading the diff. The verdict is written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md.

I ran the probes in a temp repo against a binary built at 2026-11-19 23:39:21, using a dead --base-url so no real request could go out:

| Probe | Result |
|---|---|
| --save-session sess.json, file holds keep | Refused with exit 2 before any request; message names the path and says it's not a yoyo session file; file still holds keep |
| --save-session ok.json, file holds [] (an empty saved session) | Run proceeded, failed only on the dead URL (exit 1), and the file was replaced with the new session JSON |
| -o out.txt, file holds keep me | stderr now says replaced out.txt |

• Same parse as the loader: the check reads the file the same way yoagent's restore_messages does (it parses the file as a list of messages). So it accepts exactly what the session loader accepts, and no second loader was written.
• Checked twice: the refusal runs at startup and again inside save_session_to at write time.
• Nothing left unconnected: every new function is called within this same diff.
• Docs: piped-mode.md now states both rules and the reasons for them.
• No change to defaults: the refusal only fires when the user names an existing file that isn't a session.

One thing you might trip over: on a failed run, -o still replaces the file, here with an empty response. That's how it worked before this change and isn't new.

